        position: "**India's largest fastener maker** and single source for special fasteners at most of its vehicle-maker customers.",
        money: "Net debt of **₹413cr** on Screener; borrowings fell to ₹625cr in March 2026 from ₹823cr, and gearing is about 0.13x. Operating cash was ₹837cr in FY26 and free cash ₹465cr. The ₹400cr of capex is paid from its own cash, and it pays out about 30% of profit. CRISIL reaffirmed its A1+ in September 2026. It sold ₹114.6cr of goods to its promoter holding company, TVS Sundram Fasteners Pvt Ltd. Promoters hold **46.9%**, down from 48.5% in September 2023; the main holding company's 46.8% is unchanged, and three small family entities have asked to be reclassified as public shareholders.",
        watch: ["Growth holding above 12% against the high second-half base.", "Wind and aerospace run-rates.", "US truck orders after the pre-buy ends."],
