        money: "Net debt of **₹329cr** on Screener; borrowings ₹354cr against about ₹20cr of cash, with bank lines about 85% used. Free cash was ₹92cr in FY26, helped by paying suppliers later (payable days rose from 99 to 135 through vendor financing). Capex of ₹150cr is funded from profits and borrowing 'as required'. It has guaranteed ₹54.6cr, likely for the Slovak unit, and bought ₹36.2cr of plant from promoter company Atlas Castalloy in FY26 (₹43.5cr in FY25). Key management pay was ₹22.2cr against ₹34.4cr of profit. CRISIL A, outlook cut to Stable in August 2026. Dividend payout 24%. Promoters hold **53.8%**, down from 55.7% in September 2023.",
        watch: ["Two quarters of 11%+ margin.", "The new Shikrapur plant starting by March 2027.", "No more plant bought from Atlas Castalloy."],
