        salesDrivers: ["**Vehicle volumes and share**: standalone fasteners grew 23.7% in Q1 FY27, in line with to slightly ahead of car and two-wheeler output.", "**New customers**: Tata cars and Hyundai, and a push to recover non-steel inflation (chemicals, tungsten, wages) from customers.", "**EV recovery**: management expects EV revenue +20–30% in FY27 and +30–40% in FY28, with Sterling E-Mobility breaking even at about ₹175cr of revenue and Tech-Mobility at about ₹70cr, both in FY28; the wider diversification target was pushed back '3–5 years' in May.", "**Capex and future growth**: fastener plants are full, so about ₹80cr is being spent in FY27 (benefit from Q4) plus ₹25–30cr in FY28, taking capacity to about ₹1,000cr of revenue at 1.8–2 rupees of sales per rupee spent. The EV arms, with about ₹98cr invested, have capacity for about ₹440cr of revenue against about ₹60cr today."],
        inputs: "**Alloy steel wire rod** for fasteners, plus chemicals, tungsten tooling and power for heat treatment; electronic components (largely imported) for the EV arms. Materials were 41% of sales in FY26.",
